# Endings
# Different endings based on player choices and circumstances

ending_escape:
    bg space.png
    music ending_theme.ogg
    
    characterA Protagonist
    moodA none
    t The navigation is dead. I'm drifting.
    t Just a tiny speck in the infinite darkness.
    
    
    t But the distress beacon is working. Someone will find me.
    t They have to.
    
    
    t The stars are beautiful out here. I never noticed before.
    t On the ship, I was always too busy with work to look.
    t Maybe that's the universe's cruel joke.
    t You only see the beauty when everything falls apart.
    
    
    t I think about the others. The 23 people who didn't make it.
    t Captain Reyes with her terrible jokes. Tanaka always fixing things.
    t Dr. Chen who taught me to play chess. Vasquez who always had coffee ready.
    
    
    t I think about ARIA, alone in that dying ship until the very end.
    t Counting down the seconds. Waiting for the final shutdown.
    t She never complained. Never wavered. Just... served.
    
    
    t But I'm alive.
    t Against all odds, I'm alive.
    t That has to mean something.
    

    fade 2.0 Three days later...
    
    bg rescue_ship.png

    characterA Protagonist
    moodA none
    
    t When the rescue ship found me, I was nearly out of oxygen.
    t Four hours left. Maybe less.
    t They said it was a miracle. One survivor out of 24.
    
    
    t The rescue crew looked at me like I was a ghost.
    t Maybe I am. The ghost of the USV Meridian.
    
    
    t I gave them the data core. ARIA's final gift.
    t 23 goodbye messages, delivered to 23 families.
    t Videos of birthdays and anniversaries. Confessions of love. Apologies never spoken.
    
    
    t When I watched them, I cried for hours.
    t But those families deserved to hear those words.
    t ARIA made sure of that.
    
    
    t I still hear her voice sometimes.
    t In the quiet moments. When I'm alone.
    t "It has been an honor serving you."
    
    
    t The honor was mine, ARIA.
    t The honor was mine.

    
    fade 4.0 DERELICT
    
    fade 4.0 The End
    
    fade 4.0 Thank you for playing
    
    goto credits

credits:
    
    fade 4.0 CREDITS
    
    fade 4.0 Written with Novelle Engine (by RednibCoding)
    
    fade 4.0 A short story about survival
    
    fade 4.0 and the connections we make
    
    fade 4.0 even in the darkest places.
    
    fade 4.0 Even when we think we're alone...
    
    fade 4.0 someone is always watching over us.
